2026-10-10T03:48:04Z  NOTE      fix: pm::Bridge no longer owns a PresetManager by value — constructed with PresetManager& and stores the reference, so a second manager is unbuildable by construction. Application injects *presetManager_ through VisualizerWindow -> VisualizerRenderer -> pm::Bridge; PresetBridge (QML) and projectM are now the two consumers of the ONE library: UI favourites/blacklist reach projectM, projectM selections reach QML.
2026-10-10T03:48:04Z  NOTE      sequencing: preset state (favourites/blacklist) loading moved from Bridge::init into Application::init BEFORE the async scan launches — the worker snapshots the favourite name sets at request time, so a scan started without them would publish a generation that clobbers every favourite with the empty sets (the two-manager design hid this hazard because the Bridge manager was populated after its OWN loadState). Bridge::scanPresets no longer walks the tree synchronously: the shared manager scan is owned by the manager worker (scanAsync coalesces with the in-flight walk; falls back to a synchronous scan only for a manager with no publish context — the standalone/test shape). Initial playback needs no manager call: the engine playlist starts at position 0 (shuffled where configured) and onPlaylistSwitched back-fills the manager; forcePreset rides selectByName pending-name mechanism applied at publish.
